{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c417","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a149e9-e523-7262-a03b-c2376ac3e32f"},"sequence":102,"recorded_at":1780531400000199,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a149e9-ecbb-7f22-9b48-df729b407e8e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01a149e9-ecbb-7f22-9b48-df729b407e8e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a149e9-ecbb-7f22-9b48-df729b407e8e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a149ea-5832-7622-94d2-80cba46820d0"},"task_id":"01a149ea-5832-7622-94d2-80cba46820d0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a149ea-5832-7622-94d2-80cba46820d0","chunk":"<read-skill-result name=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /Users/aazhiry1/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///Users/aazhiry1/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests/skills/durable-test-collateral/SKILL.md\nsource: bundled\nbytes_returned: 4802\nbytes_total: 4802\ntruncated: false\nnote: a skill body names entry points, not resolved behavior: before describing what named code does or ultimately runs, read that code and any saved record or setting that decides the outcome. Answer with the entry point and the concrete final result for this session in plain words. Do not replay the helpers, templates, or file citations in between, and never leave a placeholder where the final result belongs.\n</metadata>\n\nRelative paths in a skill body resolve against that skill's directory (the `skill-dir` value on its wrapper, or the parent of SKILL.md); use absolute paths in tool calls.\n\n<skill-body id=\"bundled:durable-test-collateral\" skill-dir=\"/Users/aazhiry1/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests/skills/durable-test-collateral\">\n---\nname: durable-test-collateral\ndescription: Load the body before the first implementation edit for a bug fix or behavior change, or when the user or governing specification makes reusable tests a deliverable. It keeps the smallest focused test with the delivered project and updates coverage when behavior changes. Do not load for greenfield work unless reusable tests are explicitly required, behavior-preserving refactors, verification-only work, plan/review/explanation/documentation/formatting/generated-output-only work, explicit no-change or no-tool work, or when the user declines tests.\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Durable Test Collateral\n\nVerification is part of the delivered project when it can prevent the same\nbehavior from breaking again. Use the project&apos;s existing framework and\nconventions.\n\nLoading this skill does not mean the current turn asked for the change. While you\nare still investigating — explaining existing behavior, or answering a design\nquestion the user raised — use commands that only read and leave the repository\nunmodified, tests included.\n\n## Keep the check with the project\n\nFor a bug fix or behavior change, add or update the smallest maintained test in\nthe repository&apos;s normal test layout that exercises the changed behavior. If a\nspecification makes a reusable suite or test category a deliverable, implement\nthat suite instead of treating it as private verification.\n\nAn inline interpreter command, heredoc, scratch script, temporary-directory\ntest, demo, or manual probe may help diagnose the problem, but it does not\nreplace the maintained test. Keep a useful self-authored test where the project\nkeeps its tests. If there is no such place, or the request restricts what the\ndelivered directory may contain, put the test outside that directory (for\nexample under `/tmp`) and name it in the report.\n\nDo not add a new test framework solely to satisfy this skill. If the repository\nhas no maintained harness and the request does not require one, disclose when\ndurable coverage would be disproportionate or infeasible and use the narrowest\nhonest verification instead.\n\nOn a later turn, update the maintained test even when the old suite remains\ngreen and the user does not repeat the test request. Cover the new behavior,\nnot merely an unrelated cleanup in the test file.\n\n## Aim the check where it can fail\n\nAssert what the request requires, not what you built, and end every probe in\nan assertion. If a probe shows a result the request forbids, fix the code, not\nthe assertion. Any input the public interface allows is in scope. If the\nrequest says the code may do something, that is allowed, not required.\n\nBug classes a happy-path check misses:\n\n- Ordering: when results must be acknowledged or shown in order, test with\n  items that finish out of order, and check that nothing is acknowledged or\n  shown before the items ahead of it.\n- Untrusted input: a sanitizer or filter must fail closed. If any step errors,\n  output nothing or escaped text, never the raw input.\n\n## Test the transition\n\nWhen a write can stay pending while a background step rewrites or cleans up\nstate, test reads while writes are still pending during that step, not only\nafter everything settles. A read that contradicts the request is a bug to fix.\n\n## Prove the maintained check\n\nObserve the authentic failure before the implementation change when it is safe\nand runnable. Then make the smallest implementation change and run the focused\nmaintained test after the final relevant source or test edit.\n\nDo not weaken or delete a real failing test to obtain green. Fix the product,\nor explain why the test&apos;s expectation is wrong before changing that\nexpectation. Do not repeat an unchanged check solely to collect evidence.\n\nRun a broad or full suite only when the user, a repository gate, or\nproportionate risk requires it. A focused regression test comes first; broad\nproof does not substitute for missing focused coverage.\n\nBefore deciding what a repository gate requires, read what the repository\ndeclares it runs: its CI workflow, its test entry points, and its root-level\nscripts listed with hidden entries included. A suite the project itself runs\nover this change is a gate, not an optional extra, and a suite that skips\nitself when its data is absent is not a green result.\n\nA runner is unavailable only after you tried to make it available. When the\nrepository ships the command that fetches or builds the missing fixture,\ncorpus, or toolchain, run that command once and then run the gate. Report the\ngate unavailable only when that attempt itself failed, and say what failed.\n\nIf the real runner is unavailable but the focused test can still be authored\nhonestly, leave the focused test in the repository and say it was not run. Do\nnot fabricate a passing result.\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","final_result":true}}}
